---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Update this date whenever the content below changes.
const lastUpdated = 'October 25, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy - How God Speaks To Us"
  description="What information How God Speaks To Us collects, why, and how to turn things off."
  canonical={`${Astro.url.origin}/privacy`}
>
  <section class="hero-safe relative bg-black text-white pt-32 pb-16 md:pt-40 md:pb-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        In short: we don't track you, we don't show ads, and we never sell or share your information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-lg text-gray-800 leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-10">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-black mb-4">Reading the site</h2>
      <p class="mb-10">
        You can read everything on this site without signing up or telling us who you are. We don't use analytics,
        advertising, or tracking cookies.
      </p>

      <h2 id="notifications" class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-black mb-4">Daily verse notifications</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        If you turn on the daily verse notifications, your phone or browser gives us a delivery address for
        notifications. That address comes from Apple, Google, Mozilla, or Microsoft, depending on your device. We
        store that address and the codes needed to send to it, and nothing else. We don't get your name, email,
        phone number, or location.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">We use it only to send one notification each morning with that day's verse.</p>
      <p class="mb-10">
        To stop them, tap <strong>Turn off daily verse notifications</strong> at the bottom of any page, and your
        address is deleted. If you turn notifications off in your phone's settings or remove the app instead, the
        address stops working and we delete it automatically.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-black mb-4">Contact form</h2>
      <p class="mb-10">
        When you send a message through the <a href="/contact" class="underline">contact page</a>, your name, email
        address, and message are emailed to us so we can reply. We don't add you to any mailing list.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-black mb-4">Saved on your device</h2>
      <p class="mb-10">
        If you install the app, pages you've opened are saved on your phone so you can read them without internet.
        The site also remembers on your device whether you closed the "Add this site to your phone" suggestion, so it
        doesn't keep asking. This stays on your device and isn't sent to us. Clearing your browser's website data
        removes it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-black mb-4">Services that help run the site</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Like any website, pages and images are delivered by other companies' computers, which see basic technical
        details such as your IP address while doing so:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-10">
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site and stores notification sign-ups.</li>
        <li><strong>Contentful</strong> stores our posts, verses, and images.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> provides the lettering used on the site.</li>
        <li><strong>Microsoft</strong> displays PowerPoint files when you view one on a resource page.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers contact form messages to our inbox.</li>
        <li><strong>Apple, Google, Mozilla, or Microsoft</strong> deliver notifications to your device, if you turn them on.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-black mb-4">Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email us at <a href="mailto:howhespeakstous@gmail.com" class="underline">howhespeakstous@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
